# Server Mode — Run SlayZone Backend on a Remote Host

**Status**: planning · **Owner**: TBD · **Commit policy**: standard (per-phase PRs preferred for big surface area; ask before merging).

This doc is a self-contained handoff. A fresh Claude Code (or human) session should be able to read this top-to-bottom and start executing without back-channel context.

---

## 1. Context — Why this exists

Today SlayZone runs entirely as an Electron desktop app. Main process owns the SQLite DB, PTY processes, agent CLI subprocesses (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, etc.), worktrees, and assets. Renderer talks to main via Electron IPC.

**Problem**: starting an agent and closing the laptop kills the agent. There is no way to leave a long-running coding task working unattended.

**Goal**: a backend that can run on a remote box (or locally), so a user can kick off an agent and walk away. First scope is *self-hosted* — the user provisions a server, points the Electron client at it, done. Hosted SaaS is not in scope.

**Concrete deliverable for scope 1**: a publishable npm package (`@slayzone/server`) runnable via `npx @slayzone/server`. The Electron app gains a "Server URL" setting; default keeps current behavior (Electron spawns server as a child process). Switching to a remote URL connects over HTTP/WS instead.

This work also makes a future web/mobile client possible, but those clients are explicitly **out of scope for now**. Electron remains the primary (and only) client.

---

## 2. Key Decisions (and what was rejected)

These were settled in the planning conversation. Do not relitigate without checking with the user.

| Decision | Chosen | Rejected | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| Multi-tenancy model | **Process-level** (N server processes on one box, each w/ own port + DB dir) | Logical (single process, `user_id` col scopes data) | Process-level is bulletproof isolation, ~zero code cost, no leak risk. Logical = ~6-8 weeks work, query-audit minefield, only worth it for hosted SaaS or sharing features. Neither in roadmap. |
| Auth | **Defer entirely** for scope 1 | Token / OAuth / password now | Server intended for trusted networks. Doc the assumption. Add later when hosting offering arrives. |
| Web/mobile client | **Out of scope** | Build alongside server | Electron is the only reliable browser-rendering surface (per CLAUDE.md). Web client is hypothetical, do not design for it. |
| PTY ownership | **Server owns** (local server → local PTY, remote → remote) | Client-owned, server proxy | Whole point is decoupling agent lifetime from client. |
| Worktree ownership | **Server owns** (same as PTY) | — | Consistent w/ PTY. Implies remote worktrees are inaccessible to local fs tools — flagged in §10 unresolved. |
| Server statefulness on restart | **PTYs die on restart** | Persistent (tmux-style detach) | Matches current Electron behavior. Big complexity add, defer. |
| Migration tool direction | **Local → remote only** | Bidirectional | Scope-1 use case is one-way move. Add reverse later if needed. |
| Offline mode | **Out of scope**, but use react-query in client refactor so it's possible later | Build offline-first now | Premature. react-query gives free path. |
| Agent CLI provisioning | **User installs on server box** (their API keys, their CLI binaries) | Server bundles them | Aligns w/ self-hosted scope 1. |
| User concept in DB | **Skipped** | `user_id` col scaffold | Process-level multi-tenancy makes it unnecessary. See first row. |

