## 4. Phased Plan

Each phase is a coherent merge unit with a verifiable end state. Don't combine phases unless you have a strong reason.

### Phase 0 — Path & port hardening

Make every fs root and bound port honor environment variables. Process-level multi-tenancy depends on this.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Create `getDataRoot()` utility. Likely lives in `packages/shared/paths/` (new) or an existing `@slayzone/shared` package — check first.
- [ ] Replace ~12 sites of `process.env.SLAYZONE_DB_DIR || app.getPath('userData')` with `getDataRoot()`.
- [ ] Fix hardcoded `Extensions/` and `browser-extensions.json` paths (browser domain).
- [ ] Audit `app.getPath()` call sites. Electron-only packages may keep them; any code destined for the server package must not depend on Electron.
- [ ] Confirm `SLAYZONE_PORT`, `SLAYZONE_MCP_PORT` honored at every bind site. Add `SLAYZONE_HOST` (default `localhost`).
- [ ] Smoke test: run two `pnpm dev` instances side-by-side with different `SLAYZONE_DB_DIR` + `SLAYZONE_PORT`. Verify zero data crossover.

**Done criteria:** can spin up two isolated dev instances on one machine.

### Phase 1 — Domain extraction (decouple from Electron)

Lift main-process logic into framework-free packages. Same code must be runnable from Electron main *or* from a plain Node process.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Per-domain audit. For each `packages/domains/*/src/main/`, list every Electron import (`app`, `BrowserWindow`, `ipcMain`, `webContents`, etc.).
- [ ] Replace `app.getPath()` with `getDataRoot()` (Phase 0 dep).
- [ ] Replace `BrowserWindow.webContents.send()` with an event-emitter abstraction. Two impls: Electron-IPC (for current desktop) and WS-broadcast (for server). Define interface in shared transport package.
- [ ] Move pure logic into `packages/domains/*/src/server/` (or rename `main` → `server` and keep Electron-specific glue in a thin wrapper). Decide naming — check existing convention.
- [ ] `packages/domains/auto-updater/` stays Electron-only.

**Done criteria:** every domain's logic compiles and runs in a plain Node process. Unit tests run without booting Electron.

### Phase 2 — Transport layer

Build HTTP + WS layer that shadows current IPC. Run both side-by-side during transition.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Create `packages/shared/transport/`. Defines: route registry (zod schemas), HTTP server adapter (likely Hono — confirm by checking what `rest-api/` already uses), WS server adapter, matching client SDK.
- [ ] Per IPC handler: define a route schema, mount HTTP endpoint, write parity test. Generate OpenAPI artifact.
- [ ] WS event protocol for streaming: PTY data, agent events, task changes, `tasks:changed` broadcasts. Must replace `notifyRenderer` + `broadcastToWindows`.
- [ ] **Compat layer**: keep IPC handlers live, register HTTP routes that delegate to the same backing functions. Both transports do identical work. This is the safety net during cutover.

**Done criteria:** every action in the app has a working HTTP/WS equivalent that produces identical DB state. Parity test matrix green.

### Phase 3 — Server package

Publishable npm package.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] New package: `packages/apps/server/`. Add to pnpm workspace.
- [ ] Add to `electron.vite.config.ts` `externalizeDepsPlugin({ exclude: [...] })` if it gets imported by the Electron main bundle (per memory: missing this breaks runtime).
- [ ] `bin/slayzone-server.js` — npm bin entry.
- [ ] `src/index.ts` — boot: bind port (`SLAYZONE_PORT`, default ?), init DB at `getDataRoot()`, start MCP, mount HTTP+WS, print banner.
- [ ] Banner must include: bound URL, data dir, version, **trusted-network warning**.
- [ ] Lifecycle: handle SIGTERM/SIGINT — drain WS, kill PTYs, close DB, exit clean.
- [ ] Config surface: `SLAYZONE_PORT`, `SLAYZONE_DB_DIR`, `SLAYZONE_HOST`, `SLAYZONE_MCP_PORT`. CLI flags as alternative to env.
- [ ] Publishing config — keep unpublished initially (`"private": true`) until ready.
- [ ] Cross-platform sanity check: macOS, Linux, Windows. Node 20 + 22.

**Done criteria:** `cd packages/apps/server && node bin/slayzone-server.js` boots, `/health` returns 200, data dir respected.

### Phase 4 — Electron client retarget

Replace IPC client with HTTP+WS client. Add server URL setting.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Add react-query (TanStack Query) to renderer. Wrap existing data hooks. (Memory note: `useTasksData` exposes `window.__slayzone_refreshData` — keep this contract working.)
- [ ] Replace IPC bindings in `packages/apps/app/src/preload/index.ts` with HTTP client wrappers. Or keep preload thin and have renderer talk HTTP directly — decide based on what's clean.
- [ ] WS client for streams (PTY, agent events, broadcasts).
- [ ] Settings UI: "Server URL" field. Default: empty (= local mode = spawn child).
- [ ] **Local mode** behavior: Electron main spawns `@slayzone/server` as a child process on app start, picks free port, points renderer at `http://localhost:<port>`. Child dies when Electron exits. (This preserves the current single-process UX.)
- [ ] **Remote mode** behavior: user enters URL, Electron skips child spawn, connects directly. Health check on connect.
- [ ] Mode-switch UX: changing URL prompts reload. Migrate-data button visible if switching from local to remote.

**Done criteria:** Electron app works identically to today in local mode (no perceptible regression). Switching to remote URL works against a `npx @slayzone/server` running elsewhere.

### Phase 5 — Migration tool

One-way: local data → running remote server.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] CLI command (likely under `packages/apps/cli/src/commands/migrate.ts` — confirm path). Invoke as `slay migrate --to <server-url>`.
- [ ] Tar local SQLite (closed cleanly first) + `assets/` + `project-icons/` + `backups/`. Worktrees: complex (often outside `userData`) — decide whether to copy or just rewrite paths.
- [ ] POST archive to server `/migrate/import`. Server validates, imports, returns receipt.
- [ ] Worktree path strategy: server-side worktree root = `getDataRoot()/worktrees/<taskId>/`. Migration rewrites `tasks.worktree_path` to match. (Open question — §10.)
- [ ] Dry-run flag: produce a report (what would copy/rewrite/skip) without writing.
- [ ] Integrity check: round-trip checksums on assets, row counts on tables.

**Done criteria:** migrate a real local userdata to a remote server, point Electron at the server, all tasks/projects/worktrees present and functional.

