## 5. Test Strategy

Comprehensive coverage was the original ask. Test layers:

| Layer | What | Where to add |
|-------|------|--------------|
| **fs/env hardening** (Ph 0) | Two server processes side-by-side, different env, zero data crossover. Extensions path derived. No hardcoded ports remain. | New unit test in shared/paths package. Smoke script under `scripts/`. |
| **Domain pkgs** (Ph 1) | Unit tests run without Electron. Real SQLite tmpfile (per project convention, no mocked DB — see memory `feedback_no_mock_db_in_tests`-style guidance). | Per-domain test files. |
| **HTTP contract** (Ph 2) | Zod schema validation per route. OpenAPI export buildable. Per-route happy path + 4xx + 5xx. | New `packages/shared/transport/` test suite. |
| **WS protocol** (Ph 2) | Event order. Backpressure (slow client doesn't OOM server). Reconnect — define behavior: fresh subscribe, no auto-replay. PTY byte fidelity (incl ANSI sequences). Resize event propagation. | New WS test suite. |
| **Compat layer** (Ph 2) | Same op via IPC vs HTTP yields identical DB state. Parity matrix per handler. This is the cutover safety net. | New parity test under `packages/apps/app/test/`. |
| **Server pkg** (Ph 3) | Boot/bind/SIGTERM/SIGINT. Port-in-use returns clean error. Trusted-net banner present in stdout. Cross-platform: macOS+Linux+Windows × Node 20/22. | New `packages/apps/server/test/`. CI matrix. |
| **Electron client retarget** (Ph 4) | Local mode: Electron spawns + connects to child server. Remote mode: connects to URL, no child. Switching modes preserves UI state where possible. react-query cache invalidation works on `tasks:changed`. | Extend `packages/apps/app/e2e/`. |
| **E2E (existing)** | Current Playwright-Electron suite must keep passing. Now exercises HTTP path under the hood. | `packages/apps/app/e2e/` — should require minimal changes if compat layer is right. |
| **Migration tool** (Ph 5) | Round-trip: local DB → server → identical content (row counts, asset checksums, worktree paths rewritten correctly). Dry-run produces report without writes. Concurrent access during migration handled or refused. | New `packages/apps/cli/test/migrate.test.ts`. |
| **Perf (light)** | 10 concurrent PTYs, 100 msg/sec WS throughput, memory ceiling stays bounded over 10 minutes. | Bench script under `scripts/`. |
| **Lifecycle** | Server kill mid-PTY-stream → client gets clean disconnect, not OOM/hang. Long-running PTY survives until client reconnect or server SIGTERM. | E2E. |

**Note on TDD** (per CLAUDE.md): for bug fixes write failing test first. For this feature work, contract tests (Phase 2) and parity tests should be written before flipping the cutover, not after.

