## 9. Boundaries — Don't Do These

- Don't add `user_id` columns. Multi-tenancy is process-level.
- Don't add auth. Trusted-network model. Document it loud, don't implement.
- Don't build a web client. Electron only.
- Don't add TLS termination. User's reverse proxy concern.
- Don't make WCV (browser panel) work over remote. Disable or fall through gracefully.
- Don't add persistent PTY (tmux-style). Out of scope.
- Don't backwards-compat shim if a clean break is fine — but during the IPC→HTTP transition, keep both transports until parity proven.
- Don't drop existing functionality to simplify a migration. Always migrate, never delete-and-rewrite.

